sequenceDiagram
  participant User as Staff / Student
  participant BFF as Next.js BFF
  participant API as Spring Identity API
  participant DB as PostgreSQL
  User->>BFF: Select Staff or Student on the landing page
  BFF-->>User: Sign-in form for the selected portal
  User->>BFF: Credentials (email and password, or student registration ID when enabled)
  Note over User,BFF: BFF checks Origin and Sec-Fetch-Site on mutations
  BFF->>API: POST /auth/login or /auth/student-id-login
  API->>DB: Verify credentials and account eligibility; start refresh session
  API-->>BFF: Access JWT and opaque refresh token
  BFF->>API: GET /auth/me (current roles)
  alt Account can access the selected portal
    BFF-->>User: HttpOnly SameSite cookies and redirect to the selected portal
  else Account lacks access to the selected portal
    BFF->>API: Revoke the newly issued session
    BFF-->>User: Return to the selected sign-in form with an access error
  end
  User->>BFF: Protected request with session cookie
  BFF->>API: Bearer JWT on server-side request
  API->>API: Check token, live session, auth version, roles and resource scope
  Note over BFF,API: Refresh rotates the opaque token and reuse revokes the session
  User->>BFF: POST /api/session/logout
  BFF->>API: Revoke the refresh session
  BFF-->>User: Expire browser cookies and return to the landing page
